\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Candidate alignment teaches grounded selection rather than an answer prior.} (a) $G_1$ evaluates retention where the world-model Top-\leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$1$} is correct, whereas $G_2$ evaluates correction where it is wrong. Candidate alignment improves both; GT-only erodes $G_1$ despite seeing the correct answers, while the final \textsc  {EGO}{} model reaches \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$42.5\%$} retention. (b) Strict SelAcc@Top-$K$ against training steps along the branching training path. All arms share the same frozen origin (\leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$21.0\%$}). Over the Prospection phase (\leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$522$} selection-CE steps) candidate alignment reaches \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$28.8\%$} whereas the answer-only control reaches only \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$21.9\%$}. \textsc  {EGO}{} then branches from the $\theta _{\mathrm  {CE}}$ adapter and trains a further \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$368$} steps of Retrospection-with-Replay ($\rho {=}0.15$), holding \leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$28.8\%$}. Base is frozen and is therefore constant by construction. Lines are guides to the eye. Candidate alignment is the step that carries the policy across the dashed frozen-WM Top-1 reference $L_0=\leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}24.2\%}$ (\leavevmode {\color  {measuredblue}$+7.8\,\mathrm  {pp}$}), and Retrospection preserves that position.\relax }}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
